## 2. What Aether software actually stores (SoA → memory banks)

From `DecoderGraph` (`src/graph.rs`):

### 2.1 Per-vertex banks (index = `NodeId`)

| Field | Width (SW) | Hardware role | Helios analog |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `parent` | `usize` | DSU parent / spanning-tree parent for peel | `v.parent` (S1) |
| `size` | `u32` | Union-by-**size** (not rank) | size table (Das) / implicit via cid tree (Helios uses min-id) |
| `parity` | `u8` | Live cluster parity π(C) at **root only** | related to `v.odd` / `v.st_odd` |
| `syndrome` | `u8` | **Frozen** measured defect; never written by `union` | `v.m` (measurement); peel uses this, not live parity |
| `is_boundary` | `u8` | Virtual boundary vertex (degree-1 DEM) | boundary flag / open-boundary PE |
| `cluster_boundary` | `u8` | Root flag: cluster touched a boundary | must be OR-merged on union (Aether-specific vs plain Helios odd-only) |

### 2.2 Per-edge banks (index = `EdgeId`)

| Field | Width (SW) | Hardware role | Helios analog |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `edge_u`, `edge_v` | `usize` | Endpoints (static after compile) | adjacency lists / neighbor ports |
| `capacity` | `u32` | \(W_e = 2\lfloor\lambda\ln((1-p)/p)\rfloor\), λ=1000 default | `e.w` (fixed at compile) |
| `growth` | `u32` | Integer growth; solid when `growth ≥ capacity` | `e.growth` (S3; Helios stores on lower-id PE) |
| `state` | enum | Empty / Solid | fully-grown bit |
| `obs_mask` | `u64` | Logical observable flips for this DEM column | correction datapath (not in Helios PE core) |

### 2.3 Global scalars

| Field | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `total_active_parity` | Count of clusters that are odd **and** not on boundary (= Helios “any `codd`” controller input, with boundary neutralization). |

**Locked software rules that hardware must preserve** (see `Docs/Progress` mistakes table):

1. Skip growth when `find(u)==find(v)` (intra-cluster).
2. Peel from frozen `syndrome[]`, never DSU-mutated `parity[]`.
3. Union-by-size + iterative two-pass path compression (or Helios min-`cid` spanning tree **if** proven equivalent for peel — do not mix without a co-sim check).
4. Unique virtual boundary PE per degree-1 DEM error (not one global boundary).
5. Active cluster ⇔ odd ∧ ¬`cluster_boundary`.

